1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
== Official Website www.kissasia.co  ==

2
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:14,780
[Connecting to You]

3
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:20,860
Jiang Chaonan.

4
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,500
Jiang Chaonan.

5
00:01:23,039 --> 00:01:24,070
Jiang Chaonan.

6
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:25,910
-Are you okay?
-How did you end up like this?

7
00:01:25,910 --> 00:01:27,250
What happened?

8
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:33,750
Why am I only wearing my underwear?

9
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,620
No one wants to see that.

10
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,050
Do you remember how you passed out?

11
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:42,750
I had a few drinks,

12
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:45,120
and I wanted to make some instant noodles.

13
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:48,000
Then I saw the ceiling leaking,
so I wanted to...

14
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,750
grab a rag and wipe it up.

15
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:53,910
Then... I don't remember.

16
00:01:53,910 --> 00:01:55,120
My head hurts.

17
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:56,660
Help me.

18
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:57,789
Can you get up?

19
00:01:57,789 --> 00:01:59,000
Help him to the sofa.

20
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,130
Come on, be careful.

21
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,870
You freaked me out.

22
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,150
Mr. Jiang.

23
00:02:09,289 --> 00:02:12,350
I checked your head,
and there are no obvious injuries.

24
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:14,270
I'll make a quick note for you.

25
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:18,150
"I'll Be Gone in the Dark,"

26
00:02:18,250 --> 00:02:20,250
"Crimes of the Future,"

27
00:02:20,250 --> 00:02:22,000
"Abnormal Psychology"...

28
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:27,790
You like reading these?

29
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:31,270
I know what you're thinking.

30
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:33,870
Studying criminal psychology
doesn't mean I'll commit a crime.

31
00:02:33,870 --> 00:02:35,470
And "abnormal" doesn't mean

32
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:37,030
"perverted."

33
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:39,130
I didn't say anything.

34
00:02:39,410 --> 00:02:40,670
Why are you so nervous?

35
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:50,250
Good thing he's fine.

36
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:52,660
We should be able to get off work on time.

37
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,540
Don't jinx it.

38
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,550
[Thread 3]

39
00:02:55,579 --> 00:03:00,370
[Illusion of Transparency:
How can I see through you?]

40
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,370
Senior.

41
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,110
If you're skipping class

42
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:14,830
just to cause a fire or get yourself hurt,

43
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:17,450
I think you'd better go back to school.

44
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:19,250
I'm so lucky.

45
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:21,130
I keep falling but never get hurt.

46
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,790
The Eight Lords must be protecting me.

47
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:26,670
Stop bothering the Eight Lords.

48
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:28,750
Oh, right.

49
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:32,720
Why did that police officer
come back with you?

50
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,370
Officer,

51
00:03:42,370 --> 00:03:43,250
what's wrong?

52
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:45,870
Did my kid disturb the neighbors again?

53
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:48,230
No, we just came by to check on you.

54
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:49,970
Do you mind if we go in?

55
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:55,250
No. Come in.

56
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:03,760
Alright.

57
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:05,760
Is he okay?

58
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,550
He has autism,

59
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,410
so he can be quite emotional.

60
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:18,620
He was being picky with his food,
so I gave him a lecture,

61
00:04:19,250 --> 00:04:20,380
and he lost control.

62
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,500
Hao, that's enough.

63
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:26,680
Sir, you should comfort him first.

64
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:27,700
Hao.

65
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:29,870
It's okay.

66
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:32,210
It's alright. Hey...

67
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,909
It's alright. It's alright.

68
00:04:33,930 --> 00:04:35,120
You're fine, okay?

69
00:04:35,370 --> 00:04:36,880
The officer said it's fine.

70
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,409
Don't be nervous. Stop crying, okay?

71
00:04:38,409 --> 00:04:39,620
Hao...

72
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,620
Sorry for disturbing the neighbors

73
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:50,540
and causing you trouble.

74
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,860
He'll calm down soon.

75
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,200
Is there anything else you want to know?

76
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:02,410
Nothing, but the neighbors
might still complain.

77
00:05:02,410 --> 00:05:03,910
You need to be more careful.

78
00:05:03,910 --> 00:05:04,730
Got it.

79
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,870
Thanks for your time. We're leaving.

80
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:10,080
Thanks.

81
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,670
Officers, what brings you here?

82
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:26,290
Are you here for Wen on the second floor?

83
00:05:26,410 --> 00:05:27,370
Yes.

84
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:31,500
Ma'am, do you know him?

85
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:35,250
Yes, he's a divorced single dad.

86
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:37,990
He's a nice guy, and he's good to his son.

87
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:40,800
So, that little boy often cries like this,

88
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,250
right?

89
00:05:41,250 --> 00:05:42,620
Yes, he often cries

90
00:05:42,620 --> 00:05:44,070
in the middle of the night.

91
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:45,930
Not just that, he also smashes things.

92
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:48,370
Okay, got it. Thanks, ma'am.

93
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:51,000
-You're welcome.
-Watch your steps.

94
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:57,140
Your student ID.

95
00:05:57,070 --> 00:05:57,930
[Lin Jiakai]

96
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:58,680
Thanks.

97
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,360
Oh, and this.

98
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,910
That police officer left it for you.

99
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:04,820
Why give me this?

100
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,280
What did he say?

101
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:11,030
It's for the scrapes you got when you fell
and rolled around on the ground that day.

102
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:14,620
Need help?

103
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:18,120
No, just a scratch.

104
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,920
I'll just apply the ointment
and put on a band-aid.

105
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:27,520
Thanks.

106
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:28,690
It's nothing.

107
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,330
You're still here.

108
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:42,000
[Psychology Department Lab]

109
00:06:38,659 --> 00:06:40,390
I'm almost done.

110
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,250
Ms. Peggy, could you take a look?

111
00:06:44,250 --> 00:06:46,620
Did I fill everything out correctly?

112
00:06:47,250 --> 00:06:50,540
Just finish it up. I trust you.

113
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:00,110
Ms. Peggy.

114
00:07:01,370 --> 00:07:02,110
Do you believe

115
00:07:02,110 --> 00:07:04,500
I can see the connections between people?

116
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,500
I do.

117
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:09,500
Why? You have no way

118
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,870
to verify what I see, do you?

119
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:18,000
Believing is a relative concept,

120
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,750
not an absolute conviction.

121
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:22,850
[Psychology Department Lab]

122
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:23,250
Buddhism says
there are 4,500 instants in a minute,

123
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:24,750
and 405,000 thoughts could arise.

124
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,030
How can you tell

125
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:27,750
if someone had a moment of doubt

126
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:31,500
even when they believed you?

127
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:38,909
Ms. Peggy, I don't think I understand.

128
00:07:38,909 --> 00:07:40,620
It means...

129
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:43,580
if you keep asking,
I'll get up and punch you.

130
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,370
At least tell me

131
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:52,000
what color the thread
above that nurse's head is,

132
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,080
so I know if I should pursue her or not.

133
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:57,390
Don't ask me every time

134
00:07:57,409 --> 00:07:58,810
you see a cute girl, okay?

135
00:07:58,930 --> 00:08:01,250
Are you sure you won't be upset
if I tell you?

136
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:03,010
I promise I won't be upset.

137
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:06,230
Honestly, there's no thread
between you two at all.

138
00:08:06,410 --> 00:08:07,910
She probably doesn't even want...

139
00:08:07,910 --> 00:08:09,560
I don't want to hear it.

140
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:17,080
Hey.

141
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:20,750
Hey. Hey!

142
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,090
My uncle texted me,

143
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:25,250
saying we have to
handle the leak ourselves.

144
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:27,610
He said it's normal
for an old house to have leak issues,

145
00:08:27,610 --> 00:08:28,940
but this is too serious.

146
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,180
He said he'll come by this afternoon.

147
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:38,039
Let's stop by the breakfast shop later.

148
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:39,500
I want to buy an egg burger. I'm starving.

149
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:43,000
Me too, and a medium iced black tea.
Your treat.

150
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,480
Why should I treat you?

151
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:47,950
I wonder who ruined
my limited-edition instant noodles.

152
00:08:51,790 --> 00:08:54,120
Why is that child crying so hard?

153
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,680
An auntie nearby told me
that he has autism.

154
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:01,500
Hey, where are you going?

155
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,410
Wait for me here. I'll be back soon.

156
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:06,790
Hey, Lin Jiakai!

157
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:10,760
I'm starving!

158
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,660
Hello, sir.

159
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:19,250
What's wrong?

160
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:21,160
Did someone report again?

161
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:24,370
We received a report,
so we're here to check on you.

162
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:27,620
This officer came last time.

163
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,360
He knows our situation.

164
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,050
But this is a report,

165
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,370
so we have to deal with it.

166
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:33,850
Can we go in?

167
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,460
Please.

168
00:09:36,790 --> 00:09:38,000
Come in.

169
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:40,540
Come on.

170
00:09:53,370 --> 00:09:56,410
Little one, are you okay?

171
00:09:56,870 --> 00:09:58,510
What happened?

172
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:03,440
-You can tell me anything.
-Hao.

173
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,620
It's okay now, alright?

174
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:12,040
I can help with your homework.

175
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:13,990
Be brave.

176
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:18,710
Don't care about what your teachers
and classmates say, okay?

177
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:29,750
Kid,

178
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,750
did anything happen to you?

179
00:10:38,870 --> 00:10:39,980
Is this enough?

180
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,010
Sorry for the trouble.

181
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:02,500
Perverted College Student,

182
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,370
why are you here?

183
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,870
Are you here for the crying kid upstairs?

184
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:09,730
Yes.

185
00:11:12,370 --> 00:11:14,120
Hey, sir.

186
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:18,000
Sir!

187
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,040
Who are you?

188
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:22,400
-Hao!
-Hey!

189
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,390
Don't run.

190
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:24,620
What happened?

191
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:25,210
Hao!

192
00:11:25,230 --> 00:11:27,170
Y-You beat that boy!

193
00:11:27,910 --> 00:11:29,440
What are you talking about?

194
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,660
Excuse me, I need to look for my son.

195
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:33,480
You hit him!

196
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,500
Who are you?

197
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:37,750
That's right.

198
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:40,040
Why did you suddenly run over here?

199
00:11:43,790 --> 00:11:44,870
Okay, forget it.

200
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,160
Dawei, let's find him first.

201
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,910
I know where to find him.

202
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:50,750
You better know where he is. Hao!

203
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,910
Dawei, Dawei!

204
00:11:59,910 --> 00:12:02,160
Are you spacing out? Hurry up!

205
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,890
Yeah, let's follow him, hurry.

206
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:09,790
Hao!

207
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,250
Dawei, follow him!

208
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:30,880
Where are you going?

209
00:12:31,370 --> 00:12:33,440
I'm looking for Hao!

210
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,250
How do you know where he is?

211
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:37,870
I just know.

212
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:00,380
Little one.

213
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:03,250
You're Hao, right?

214
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:10,160
You don't want to go home

215
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,690
because of your dad, right?

216
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:20,540
Okay, it's fine. We can stay here for now.

217
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,920
Can you show me your hand?

218
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,220
No bruises?

219
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,440
How's that possible?

220
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,840
Can I check your body?

221
00:14:08,810 --> 00:14:09,900
I'll make a call.

222
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:23,870
Little one.

223
00:14:28,250 --> 00:14:29,190
Hey,

224
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:32,030
I'll take you back
to put on some medicine, okay?

225
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:33,780
No.

226
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:37,070
I won't take you home.

227
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,790
We'll go to the hospital and see a doctor.

228
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:42,120
Don't worry.

229
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,890
We found Hao in the park nearby.

230
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,220
There really are bruises on his body
from being beaten.

231
00:14:54,250 --> 00:14:55,790
Take his dad

232
00:14:55,790 --> 00:14:57,150
back to the station.

233
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,690
Let's go to the hospital.

234
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:05,040
Okay.

235
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,900
This officer will take you to the hospital.

236
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,080
Can you get up?

237
00:15:10,510 --> 00:15:11,580
Watch your head.

238
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:19,580
What's wrong?

239
00:15:22,370 --> 00:15:23,370
Let's go.

240
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,050
Just follow him.

241
00:15:45,010 --> 00:15:46,410
Why are you still here?

242
00:15:46,770 --> 00:15:48,830
Aren't you done with your statement?

243
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:52,840
I just wanted to know

244
00:15:52,870 --> 00:15:55,250
how the questioning with his dad went.

245
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:57,560
Did he admit to the abuse?

246
00:15:58,370 --> 00:15:59,180
Yes.

247
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:04,000
He said he couldn't stand

248
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,500
Hao's emotional reactions
caused by his autism,

249
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,230
so he lost control and beat him.

250
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:09,770
But we didn't find

251
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:11,700
any medical records of his autism.

252
00:16:12,370 --> 00:16:14,620
We'll arrange
a new medical assessment for Hao

253
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:16,950
to find out whether he actually has autism

254
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
or if his abnormal social responses

255
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:23,120
are caused by the abuse.

256
00:16:26,870 --> 00:16:29,370
No matter how much
his dad says he regrets it,

257
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,120
or how much Hao wants to see his dad,

258
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:33,830
I think...

259
00:16:33,850 --> 00:16:36,510
it's best that they live separately
from now on.

260
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:38,690
Why?

261
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,320
Because when I saw them

262
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:45,660
walking on the street together,

263
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,370
I saw the blue thread.

264
00:16:57,370 --> 00:16:58,620
So, I thought

265
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:00,540
that maybe his dad
wasn't really good to him.

266
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:03,400
He was just pretending it
in front of the neighbors.

267
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,609
But the saddest part is...

268
00:17:06,010 --> 00:17:08,000
even though his dad treats him like this,

269
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,000
he doesn't hate his dad.

270
00:17:18,369 --> 00:17:19,339
Okay, got it.

271
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:24,410
I know you don't believe this, right?

272
00:17:24,869 --> 00:17:27,250
I'll let you know if there's any progress.

273
00:17:28,119 --> 00:17:30,120
Just go back and rest.

274
00:17:45,890 --> 00:17:53,630
[Qishi Police Station]

275
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,140
What's this?

276
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,910
That college student left it

277
00:18:04,910 --> 00:18:06,660
and asked us to give it to Hao.

278
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:08,420
He said if anything happens,

279
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,620
Hao can call him.

280
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:11,220
He lives nearby and can help.

281
00:18:11,410 --> 00:18:13,620
I thought he was just some
immature college kid.

282
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:15,020
Turns out he's so kind.

283
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,620
Did the water pipe burst?

284
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,500
Why is it leaking so much?

285
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:26,750
How would I know?

286
00:18:26,750 --> 00:18:28,290
I just called my uncle.

287
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:31,460
He said this place is ruined
and has to be restored.

288
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,330
He told us to move somewhere else
for two months.

289
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:35,870
He wants to completely renovate it.

290
00:18:35,870 --> 00:18:37,160
Move somewhere else?

291
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:39,070
Where are we supposed to go?

292
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:40,080
No idea.

293
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:42,700
Maybe go to a relative's place
in Taipei, or...

294
00:18:44,910 --> 00:18:47,510
You don't have any relatives
in Taipei, right?

295
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:48,660
No.

296
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:51,520
Maybe you can apply for
a temporary dorm or something.

297
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:53,910
It's too late to apply for it.

298
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:56,190
And I don't want to live too far away.

299
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:59,100
It'd be too inconvenient
for my part-time job.

300
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:02,260
Poor you.

301
00:19:13,790 --> 00:19:15,370
Who is this?

302
00:19:17,410 --> 00:19:18,460
Chief?

303
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,370
Chief?

304
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,610
Why are they so expensive?

305
00:19:27,690 --> 00:19:32,460
[Peipei Rental]

306
00:19:32,490 --> 00:19:34,530
[One-Bedroom Unit with Balcony]

307
00:19:39,290 --> 00:19:40,870
It's you.

308
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,000
What would you like today?

309
00:19:49,410 --> 00:19:51,440
Three iced lattes to go.

310
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,000
Three iced lattes.

311
00:19:54,290 --> 00:19:55,610
Anything else?

312
00:19:55,630 --> 00:19:56,880
That's all.

313
00:19:57,250 --> 00:19:59,660
210 TWD in total.

314
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,700
That's 300 TWD.

315
00:20:09,270 --> 00:20:11,060
Here's 90 TWD change.

316
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:17,000
How did you get this?

317
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:19,660
Do you also hit on little boys now?

318
00:20:20,410 --> 00:20:21,410
No.

319
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,130
I told your colleagues my intentions.

320
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:28,410
I know. Don't be so nervous.

321
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:31,040
As for Hao,

322
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:33,750
we've officially reported it
to the social welfare agency.

323
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:35,040
Don't worry.

324
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,620
Are you looking for an apartment?

325
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:42,870
Yes.

326
00:20:43,250 --> 00:20:45,750
My landlord is taking it back
for renovations,

327
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:48,370
so I need a place to stay for two months.

328
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,950
But short-term rentals are so expensive.

329
00:20:51,370 --> 00:20:53,250
I asked a few friends,

330
00:20:53,250 --> 00:20:56,120
but none of them can help.

331
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:59,830
Actually, Jiang Chaonan
has been asking around for you.

332
00:21:00,250 --> 00:21:02,650
You only need to stay
for two months, right?

333
00:21:02,870 --> 00:21:03,750
Yes.

334
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:05,370
The landlord said

335
00:21:05,370 --> 00:21:08,570
we can move back sooner
if the renovations are done early.

336
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:13,000
Well, I have a room

337
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,620
that the landlord uses for storage.

338
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:18,120
With a little cleaning,
it could work as a bedroom.

339
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,910
If it's only for two months,

340
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:22,620
you can stay there.

341
00:21:55,290 --> 00:21:58,240
[Peggy Talks Love Psychology]

342
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:58,000
Everyone's online.

343
00:21:58,030 --> 00:21:59,540
This is Two-Minute Love Live Stream.

344
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,380
[Two-Minute Love Live Stream]

345
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:01,540
It's fleeting, so don't miss it.

346
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:03,410
I'm Ms. Peggy.

347
00:22:03,410 --> 00:22:03,980
Today,

348
00:22:04,010 --> 00:22:04,900
I'm going to talk about

349
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:07,080
the illusion of transparency.

350
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:10,200
Illusion of transparency.

351
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:10,880
This is

352
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:12,200
a cognitive bias.

353
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:13,060
[Cognitive Bias]

354
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,170
We often overestimate

355
00:22:13,170 --> 00:22:14,000
our understanding

356
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:14,740
of other people's

357
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:16,290
mental states

358
00:22:16,290 --> 00:22:16,720
or

359
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:17,330
other people's understanding

360
00:22:17,330 --> 00:22:18,410
of our mental states.

361
00:22:18,410 --> 00:22:20,290
Like right now.

362
00:22:20,290 --> 00:22:22,700
This is a question from Student A.

363
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:24,410
Student A said,

364
00:22:24,410 --> 00:22:27,410
"My boyfriend would rather play games
than have dinner with me.

365
00:22:27,410 --> 00:22:29,790
I was so mad
and ignored him for three days.

366
00:22:29,790 --> 00:22:30,960
And he actually said he didn't know

367
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:32,410
what I was angry about."

368
00:22:32,410 --> 00:22:33,030
Well,

369
00:22:33,050 --> 00:22:33,970
this is what we call

370
00:22:33,970 --> 00:22:35,700
the illusion of transparency.

371
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:36,950
You were very angry,

372
00:22:36,950 --> 00:22:38,040
but you didn't explain it clearly.

373
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:39,410
So, he had no idea

374
00:22:39,410 --> 00:22:41,160
what you were angry about,

375
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,000
right?

376
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:42,550
Even if

377
00:22:42,570 --> 00:22:43,290
you've been

378
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,030
together

379
00:22:44,060 --> 00:22:45,290
for a long time,

380
00:22:45,290 --> 00:22:46,700
it doesn't mean

381
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,380
you'll be so connected

382
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:48,800
that you can even

383
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:51,290
read each other's minds, okay?

384
00:22:51,290 --> 00:22:52,010
When there's a problem,

385
00:22:52,010 --> 00:22:53,580
you need to talk it out.

386
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,220
In a relationship,

387
00:22:54,220 --> 00:22:54,840
you must

388
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:56,500
communicate with each other.

389
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:56,400
[Communicate with Each Other]

390
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,000
That's how it lasts,

391
00:22:58,020 --> 00:22:58,620
okay?

392
00:22:58,620 --> 00:22:59,530
And stop messaging me

393
00:22:59,530 --> 00:23:00,370
over and over.

394
00:23:00,370 --> 00:23:01,500
One message is enough.

395
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:02,700
Thanks.

396
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:03,700
Love you.
